# Backend Fundamentals

Learning REST API development with Python and FastAPI.

## Progress

### Week 1 — API Foundations
- Understood what a REST API is and how HTTP requests work
- Built first endpoint returning JSON
- Implemented full CRUD API for a task list
  - GET /tasks — retrieve all tasks
  - GET /tasks/{id} — retrieve single task
  - POST /tasks — create a task with request body validation
  - PUT /tasks/{id} — mark a task as complete
  - DELETE /tasks/{id} — remove a task
- Learned Pydantic models for request body validation
- Understood HTTP methods, status codes, and JSON formatting rules
- Connected API to PostgreSQL database hosted on Neon (AWS)

## Tech Stack
- Python 3.11
- FastAPI
- Uvicorn
- Pydantic
- SQLAlchemy
- PostgreSQL (Neon)

## What's Next
- Create database tables and migrate from in-memory storage
- Full persistent CRUD using real SQL queries
- Authentication with JWT

## Known Limitations
- Data still stored in memory — database connected but not yet used for queries
- Restarting server wipes all current task data
- No authentication yet

## Key Concepts Learned
- REST architecture and HTTP methods
- Why databases are necessary over in-memory storage
  - Persistence across server restarts
  - Safe concurrent access via transactions
  - Single source of truth across multiple server instances
  - Efficient querying and normalisation at scale
